		{
			dependencies: [
				"6E06FDD802380DCB"
			]
			description: [
				"Liquid air is cryogenic. Steel and iron pipes, pumps and tanks frost white, then crack and burst, and PVC fares no better. Copper, aluminium and glass take it, and tooltips say what cracks."
				""
				"Spilt, it boils off in seconds, freezing the water beside it."
			]
			id: "5CDB9FE65D68D6E3"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Cold enough to crack steel"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "0C9EA2B4F9F6B25F"
					item: "mcremix:liquid_air_bucket"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Liquid Air"
			x: 1.75d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"5CDB9FE65D68D6E3"
			]
			description: [
				"Aluminium Column Sections join like steel ones, but need no heat and no condenser: to liquid air, the world is a furnace. Nitrogen comes off the top, oxygen the bottom and argon a section of its own between. Spare sections sit just under the top and draw nothing, and goggles show which section draws what."
				""
				"Argon and oxygen boil only 3 °C apart, so the column needs extra sections between them, or liquid nitrogen piped back into its top as reflux. It frosts up and grows icicles as it runs, and melts beside anything &6Hot&r."
			]
			id: "4A92C81CCC100231"
			rewards: [ ]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "Boiled by the world's warmth"
			tasks: [
				{
					icon: "mcremix:aluminium_column_section"
					id: "6D7B9EB28CE4A5E8"
					observe_type: 2
					timer: 10L
					title: "Look at an air column grown icicles"
					to_observe: "mcremix:aluminium_column_section[frost=2]"
					type: "observation"
				}
			]
			title: "The Air Column"
			x: 3.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"4A92C81CCC100231"
			]
			description: [
				"Pipe oxygen into a lit Steel Furnace beside its fuel and the fire burns twice as hot, its ceiling a level higher. Let loose, oxygen makes fire spread."
